.TH ORGANIZE 1 "2026-10-24" "organize 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
organize \- sort the files of a directory into category subfolders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B organize
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B organize
moves the regular files that sit directly inside
.I DIRECTORY
into subfolders chosen from the file extension.
The default
.I DIRECTORY
is the current directory.
.PP
Only the top level of
.I DIRECTORY
is read. Hidden files, subdirectories and symbolic links are never
moved. Subfolders are created on demand, so a directory that only holds
images ends up with a single
.I Images
subfolder.
.PP
A file is never overwritten. If the destination name is already taken,
a numeric suffix is inserted before the extension:
.I photo.jpg
becomes
.I photo_1.jpg
and then
.I photo_2.jpg
on the next collision. Compound archive extensions are kept whole, so
.I backup.tar.gz
becomes
.I backup_1.tar.gz
and not
.IR backup.tar_1.gz .
.PP
Files are processed in byte order of their names, which makes a run
reproducible for a given directory content.
.PP
Files that a download manager is still writing are always skipped, even
when
.B \-\-others
is given:
.IR .part ,
.IR .crdownload ,
.IR .download ,
.I .tmp
and
.IR .filepart .
.PP
.I DIRECTORY
is refused when it is a system directory or the root of a git
repository. The check is an exact match on the resolved path, so
.I $HOME
is refused while
.I $HOME/Downloads
is allowed, and a subdirectory of a repository is allowed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-preview
Print the planned moves without touching the filesystem. It can be
combined with the category options.
.TP
.B \-\-images
Only handle the
.I Images
category. Files of the other categories stay where they are.
.TP
.B \-\-documents
Only handle the
.I Documents
category.
.TP
.B \-\-music
Only handle the
.I Music
category.
.TP
.B \-\-videos
Only handle the
.I Videos
category.
.TP
.B \-\-archives
Only handle the
.I Archives
category.
.TP
.B \-\-others
Only handle the
.I Others
category.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-device
Print the storage device, mount point, filesystem and free space of
.IR DIRECTORY ,
then exit without moving any file. It does not move anything, so it is
allowed on a refused directory.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options. Use it when
.I DIRECTORY
starts with a hyphen.
.PP
Options must appear before
.IR DIRECTORY .
Without a category option every category is handled.
.SH CATEGORIES
The extension match is case insensitive and ignores the leading dot.
.TP
.B Images
jpg, jpeg, png, gif, bmp, webp, svg, tif, tiff, heic, avif
.TP
.B Documents
pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, md, rtf, odt, ods, odp,
csv, epub
.TP
.B Music
mp3, wav, flac, aac, ogg, m4a, opus, wma
.TP
.B Videos
mp4, mkv, avi, mov, webm, m4v, wmv, flv
.TP
.B Archives
zip, rar, 7z, tar, gz, bz2, xz, tgz, iso
.TP
.B Others
every file that matches none of the above, including files without an
extension
.SH OUTPUT
One line per moved file, in the form
.RI "name " "-> " "Category/name" .
In preview mode each line starts with
.IR "[preview] " .
A summary line follows:
.RS
.EX
Moved 12 files: Images 5, Documents 4, Music 1, Videos 1, Archives 1.
.EE
.RE
.PP
Only non-empty categories appear in the summary. A preview prints
.RI "12 files would be moved" " instead."
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every file was moved, or there was nothing to move.
.TP
.B 1
At least one file could not be moved. The remaining files were still
processed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid option or argument.
.TP
.B 3
.I DIRECTORY
does not exist or is not a directory.
.TP
.B 4
.I DIRECTORY
is a system directory or the root of a git repository.
.SH EXAMPLES
Sort the current directory:
.PP
.RS
.EX
organize
.EE
.RE
.PP
Preview what would happen, without moving anything:
.PP
.RS
.EX
organize --preview
.EE
.RE
.PP
Sort only the images of another folder:
.PP
.RS
.EX
organize --images ~/Downloads
.EE
.RE
.PP
Show which storage device holds the files, and how much space is left:
.PP
.RS
.EX
organize --device ~/Downloads
.EE
.RE
.PP
Sort another folder, whose name starts with a hyphen:
.PP
.RS
.EX
organize -- -incoming
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mv (1),
.BR mkdir (1)
